          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.517,
            0.849,
            0.594
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Some examples of exponential growth we have seen earlier in this chapter are ‘The Stones that Shine’, ‘Magical Pond’, ‘How Many Combinations’. We shall explore more such interesting examples in a later chapter and also in the next grade."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.603,
            0.849,
            0.643
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Can you come up with some examples of linear growth and of exponential growth?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.662,
            0.576,
            0.684
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Getting a Sense for Large Numbers"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.693,
            0.848,
            0.768
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Last year, we learnt about lakhs and crores, as well as millions and billions. A lakh is 10"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (1,00,000), a crore is 10"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (1,00,00,000), and an arab is 10"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (1,00,00,00,000), whereas a million is 10"
